course: dictionary
lesson: 3233
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning is right. «Marmot families live in big burrows with many entrances.» Here entrances are the openings where the marmots go in and out.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «The actor made a grand entrance onto the stage.» Here entrance means the act of coming in, not a door. Ask yourself: which meaning would fit this sentence?
explain: Entrance can also be a verb, and then it means to fill someone with wonder. «The singer's voice entranced the whole crowd.» The crowd was not going in anywhere. They were delighted and amazed, held still by the music.
fact: An entrance is a door, gate or opening where you go into a place.
fact: An entrance can also be the act of coming in, like an actor coming on stage.
fact: An entrance fee is the money you pay for the right to go in.
fact: To entrance someone means to fill them with wonder. As a verb, it is stressed on «TRANCE».
fact: Useful phrases: «the main entrance», «make an entrance», «entrance exam».
exercise: «Marmot families live in big burrows with many entrances.» What are the entrances here? | Actors coming on stage | Money paid to go in | *Openings where the marmots go in and out | Feelings of wonder
exercise: «The actor made a grand entrance onto the stage.» What does entrance mean in this sentence? | Something very dull | *The act of coming in | The money you pay to go in | A door or gate
exercise: «The lights are brighter at the entrance so drivers' eyes can get used to the dark.» Where is the entrance? | *At the place where drivers go in | Under the water | In the middle of the road | At the top of the tunnel
test: «The entrance fee for the zoo is five pounds.» What does entrance fee mean? | The gate that opens at night | *The money you pay to go in | A map of the zoo | The way out of the zoo
test: «The singer's voice entranced the whole crowd.» What does entranced mean here? | Angry | *Filled with wonder and delight | Bored | Tired
exam: «A good meeting point is easy to find, such as a big sign or the entrance gate.» What does entrance gate mean? | A fee you must pay | A kind of sign | Coming on stage | *A gate where you go in
